    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0518" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6231/319</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-13">March 13, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During the call of the German Ambassador he introduced the subject relating to
                    the time of entering upon negotiations for a new or revised reciprocity treaty
                    between our two Governments. I stated to him that I could not take up the
                    question of time except to say that I would be glad to urge that, as early as
                    practical after the passage of the pending legislation in Congress giving the
                    Executive authority to negotiate these treaties, I would call together my
                    associates who are dealing directly with reciprocity negotiations and we would
                    discuss our plans and program, including Germany and other Governments seeking
                    early negotiations, and do the best possible relative to suggesting an early
                    date to commence conversations with the German Government; that in the meantime
                    the Ambassador and his associates at the Embassy might keep in touch with my
                    associates, as well as myself, here in the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ull</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
